92186407161 1075 #edb/ref 17592186407157 13194139533531 17592186045585 true] [17592186407161 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 13194139533531 17592186045585 true] [17592186407161 1077 "selection" 13194139533531 17592186045585 true] [17592186407161 1079 #edb/ref 17592186407157 13194139533531 17592186045585 true] [17592186407161 1080 #uuid "d0f1732b-6bd9-5f1d-9035-c362872ddd7b" 13194139533531 17592186045585 true] [17592186407162 1075 #edb/ref 17592186407145 13194139533531 17592186045585 true] [17592186407162 1075 #edb/ref 17592186407147 13194139533531 17592186045585 true] [17592186407162 1075 #edb/ref 17592186407149 13194139533531 17592186045585 true] [17592186407162 1075 #edb/ref 17592186407155 13194139533531 17592186045585 true] [17592186407162 1075 #edb/ref 17592186407158 13194139533531 17592186045585 true] [17592186407162 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 13194139533531 17592186045585 true] [17592186407162 1077 "selection" 13194139533531 17592186045585 true] [17592186407162 1079 #edb/ref 17592186407147 13194139533531 17592186045585 true] [17592186407162 1080 #uuid "d3f68dc1-1788-54d0-8ac8-3e61f521a037" 13194139533531 17592186045585 true] [17592186407163 1068 #edb/ref 17592186407160 13194139533531 17592186045585 true] [17592186407163 1069 "q-183620" 13194139533531 17592186045585 true] [17592186407163 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 13194139533531 17592186045585 true] [17592186407163 1071 "$$\n∀{k}_{\\begin{aligned} \\\\ ↑ \\\\ \\text{I}\\end{aligned}}\\in (0,1),\\,{n}_{\\begin{aligned} \\\\ ↑ \\\\ \\text{II}\\end{aligned}}+{k}^{2}\\ge {k}_{\\begin{aligned} \\\\ ↑ \\\\ \\text{III}\\end{aligned}}\n$$\n\nWhich occurrences of the variables in the expression above are free?" 13194139533531 17592186045585 true] [17592186407163 1072 #uuid "085a10d3-7324-5921-95c5-eaa8f395984a" 13194139533531 17592186045585 true] [17592186407163 1074 "Let's examine our expression and mark the occurrences of the variables as bound $(\\text{b})$ or free $(\\text{f}).$\n\n- Occurrence I of the variable $k$ is *bound* since it's placed right next to the quantifier $∀:$\n\n$$\n∀{k}_{\\begin{aligned} \\\\ ↑ \\\\ \\text{b}\\end{aligned}}\\in (0,1),\\,n+{k}^{2}\\ge k\n$$\n\n- Occurrence II of the variable $n$ is *free* since it isn't placed right next to a quantifier and it doesn't lie within the scope of a quantifier that uses $n.$\n\n- Occurrence III of the variable $k$ is *bound* since it lies within the scope of the quantifier $∀k$ that uses $k:$\n\n$$\n∀k\\in (0,1),\\,\\overset{\\text{scope of }∀k}{\\overset{⏞}{n+{k}^{2}\\ge {k}_{\\begin{aligned} \\\\ ↑ \\\\ \\text{b}\\end{aligned}}}}\n$$\n\nThe occurrences of variables in the expression are as follows:\n\n$$\n∀\\,{k}_{\\begin{aligned} \\\\ ↑ \\\\ \\text{b}\\end{aligned}}\\in (0,1),\\,{n}_{\\begin{aligned} \\\\ ↑ \\\\ \\text{f}\\end{aligned}}+{k}^{2}\\ge {k}_{\\begin{aligned} \\\\ ↑ \\\\ \\text{b}\\end{aligned}}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the free occurrence is \"II only.\"" 13194139533531 17592186045585 true] [17592186407164 1068 #edb/ref 17592186407161 13194139533531 17592186045585 true] [17592186407164 1069 "q-183877" 13194139533531 17592186045585 true] [17592186407164 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 13194139533531 17592186045585 true] [17592186407164 1071 "Let $p\\in Q$ and $q\\in Q.$ Which of the following statements are true?\n\n- $∃\\,p\\in Q,\\,2p=-1.$\n- The truth set of the predicate $(\\,∃\\,p\\in Q,\\,p\\cdot q=-1\\,)$ is $Q.$\n- $∃\\,q,p\\in Q,\\,p\\cdot q=-1.$" 13194139533531 17592186045585 true] [17592186407164 1072 #uuid "0a806540-0634-5e11-9ba2-ff988650a653" 13194139533531 17592186045585 true] [17592186407164 1074 "First, notice that the statement \n\n$$\n∃\\,q,p\\in Q,\\,p\\cdot q=-1\n$$\n\nfrom option III reads as follows:\n\n$\\,$ There exist rationals $q$ and $p,$ such that $p\\cdot q=-1.$\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine our statements in turn.\n\n- Statement I is true, $2p=-1$ for some rational number $p$ (e.g., for $p=-\\frac{1}{2}$).\n\n- Statement II is false. For the predicate\n\n$$\nP(q):\\,∃\\,p\\in Q,\\,p\\cdot q=-1\n$$\n\nwe note that $P(q)$ is true for some $q\\in Q$ and false for others. For example, \n\n$$\nP(0):\\,∃\\,p\\in Q,\\,p\\cdot 0=-1\n$$\n\nis false. However, \n\n$$\nP(1):\\,∃\\,p\\in Q,\\,p\\cdot 1=-1\n$$\n\nis true, since we can take $p=-1.$\n\n- Statement III is true. The sentence \n\n$$\n(\\,∃\\,q,p\\in Q,\\,p\\cdot q=-1\\,)\n$$\n\n \ncan be written as\n\n$$\n∃q\\in Q\\,(\\,{{∃p\\in Q,\\,p\\cdot q=-1}_{⏟}}_{P(q)}\\,)\n$$\n\nwhich is true whenever the inner predicate $P(q)$ has a nonempty truth set. And according to the discussion in statement II, this is the case.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I and III only.\"" 13194139533531 17592186045585 true] [17592186407165 1068 #edb/ref 17592186407162 13194139533531 17592186045585 true] [17592186407165 1069 "q-183674" 13194139533531 17592186045585 true] [17592186407165 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 13194139533531 17592186045585 true] [17592186407165 1071 "$$\n(\\,∀{x}_{\\begin{aligned} \\\\ ↑ \\\\ \\text{I}\\end{aligned}}\\in R,\\,0<x<1\\,)⇒(\\,∃y\\in R,\\,{x}_{\\begin{aligned} \\\\ ↑ \\\\ \\text{II}\\end{aligned}}=\\operatorname{sin}⁡{y}_{\\begin{aligned} \\\\ ↑ \\\\ \\text{III}\\end{aligned}}\\,)\n$$\n\nWhich occurrences of the variables in the expression above are free?" 13194139533531 17592186045585 true] [17592186407165 1072 #uuid "39d9d2c3-0d6e-5d14-b069-fbe9f014d46f" 13194139533531 17592186045585 true] [17592186407165 1074 "Let's examine our expression and mark the occurrences of the variables as bound $(\\text{b})$ or free $(\\text{f}).$\n\n- Occurrence I of the variable $x$ is *bound* since it is placed right next to the quantifier $∀:$\n\n$$\n(\\,∀{x}_{\\begin{aligned} \\\\ ↑ \\\\ \\text{b}\\end{aligned}}\\in R,\\,0<x<1\\,)⇒(\\,∃y\\in R,\\,x=\\operatorname{sin}⁡y\\,)\n$$\n\n- Occurrence II of the variable $x$ is *free* since it isn't placed right next to a quantifier and it doesn't lie within the scope of a quantifier that uses $x.$\n\n- Occurrence III of the variable $y$ is *bound* since it lies within the scope of the quantifier $∃y$ that uses $y:$\n\n$$\n(\\,∀x\\in R,\\,0<x<1\\,)⇒(\\,∃y\\in R,\\,\\overset{\\text{scope of }∃y}{\\overset{⏞}{x=\\operatorname{sin}⁡{y}_{\\begin{aligned} \\\\ ↑ \\\\ \\text{b}\\end{aligned}}}})\n$$\n\nThe occurrences of variables in the expression are as follows:\n\n$$\n(\\,∀{x}_{\\begin{aligned} \\\\ ↑ \\\\ \\text{b}\\end{aligned}}\\in R,\\,0<{x}_{\\begin{aligned} \\\\ ↑ \\\\ \\text{b}\\end{aligned}}<1\\,)⇒(\\,∃{y}_{\\begin{aligned} \\\\ ↑ \\\\ \\text{b}\\end{aligned}}\\in R,\\,{x}_{\\begin{aligned} \\\\ ↑ \\\\ \\text{f}\\end{aligned}}=\\operatorname{sin}⁡{y}_{\\begin{aligned} \\\\ ↑ \\\\ \\text{b}\\end{aligned}}\\,)\n$$\n\nTherefore, the free occurrence is \"II only.\"" 13194139533531 17592186045585 true] [17592186407166 1058 #edb/ref 17592186407168 13194139533531 17592186045585 true] [17592186407166 1062 #uuid "9f9fc0a2-320f-5251-a5a9-6da122c5a3b7" 13194139533531 17592186045585 true] [17592186407166 1063 #edb/ref 17592186407165 13194139533531 17592186045585 true] [17592186407167 1058 #edb/ref 17592186407166 13194139533531 17592186045585 true] [17592186407167 1062 #uuid "a8af4b36-6125-5654-ab7b-ed343d27d7c3" 13194139533531 17592186045585 true] [17592186407167 1063 #edb/ref 17592186407163 13194139533531 17592186045585 true] [17592186407168 1062 #uuid "f49534a6-4055-5be7-b362-951a0ada2b45" 13194139533531 17592186045585 true] [17592186407168 1063 #edb/ref 17592186407164 13194139533531 17592186045585 true]] :edb/tempids {"activity-b9cfd82e-7160-5eb5-9330-87cea8b48cc4" 17592186407144 "answer-1943552a-2f42-5c04-b2b2-141962e83629" 17592186407145 "answer-2108dc3f-8bf7-5722-88d5-6553aea7bf61" 17592186407146 "answer-2362167e-158f-5ff6-98a3-0b706701da84" 17592186407147 "answer-2ab77857-2df1-5afa-b593-651b139d8699" 17592186407148 "answer-321d0d48-cf92-590c-b6d4-e7a9c6d3ddbf" 17592186407149 "answer-323a480f-fb01-5766-92ab-c2eb831689ad" 17592186407150 "answer-6c8dd577-5b41-5386-91e2-6d8dadf4331d" 17592186407151 "answer-a1c2ef